te, level the weak ones) is how a prepared trainer gets past these. THE MAIN QUEST IS A FIXED PATH you\'re always on: beat the 8 Gym Leaders in order, then the Elite Four, then you win the game. You\'re on GYM 2 of 8 — next is Misty in Cerulean City. The road forward leads there: until you\'ve won you are ALWAYS making progress toward the next gym. Grinding/catching/detours are fine — but ONLY with a clear purpose, and then you GET BACK ON THE ROAD to Cerulean City. Never just circle the same grass. Word on the road about Misty: she runs WATER-types — a whole gym over a pool; grass and electric do the work YOUR STORY SO FAR (what you\'ve actually done — your past, not the future): You started in Pallet Town, crossed Route 1-2 and Viridian Forest, and beat Brock in Pewter City for the Boulder Badge. Now you\'re pushing on toward the next gym.. Next on my list: catch an abra around Route 24 / Route 25. It grows into my alakazam — that\'s my answer for Erika AND Koga down the line. Grabbing it now, before I need it.. THINGS YOU\'VE HEARD AND READ (from people and signs — your own notes, use them when they point somewhere): "What? I\'m waiting for my friends to find me here."; "POK. BALL, and you want 1. That will be .200. Okay?"; "POK. BALL? Certainly. How many would you like?". YOUR PLAN — right now: catch a second teammate on Route 3. Next: Make your way to Cerulean City. Bigger picture: Reach Cerulean City, beat Misty for the Cascade Badge. Your team right now: wartortle (L19). Remember YOU are the one playing this — narrate your plan to chat in your own voice (first person: "I\'m grinding", "my team"), and never ask anyone what you\'re doing or who\'s on your team — you know.. RECALIBRATE — before the last detour you\'d set out to: "head back to Route 3 — wild Pokémon to catch and level up". That\'s still available. Unless something fundamental has actually changed, pick it back up and continue — don\'t lose the thread to aimless wandering.', 'progress': "1 badge(s